   "subject": "latent factor residual",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>Hi all,</div><div>  In my model, I want to use latent factor residual/error term to predict another latent factor, can we do that in lavaan? If someone in lavaan community knows how to do it, can you share your knowledge with me, thank you so much. <br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "LBc3RCnlAAAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2024-01-11T11:42:19Z",
   "subject": "Re: latent factor residual",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div>I want to use latent factor residual/error term to predict another latent factor, can we do that in lavaan? </div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div><div>Yes, just define an orthogonal factor that &quot;absorbs&quot; all the residual variance, by setting the residual variance to zero.</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);background:none;white-space:pre;word-break:normal;line-height:1.5;overflow:auto\"><span style=\"background:none;word-spacing:normal;word-break:normal;line-height:1.5\"><font face=\"Courier New\">model <span style=\"color:rgb(154,110,58);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)\">&lt;-</span> &#39; \r\n  <span style=\"color:slategray\"># latent variable definitions</span>\r\n     ind60 <span style=\"color:rgb(154,110,58);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(154,110,58);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)\">~</span> x1 <span style=\"color:rgb(154,110,58);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)\">+</span> x2 <span style=\"color:rgb(154,110,58);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)\">+</span> x3\r\n     dem60 <span style=\"color:rgb(154,110,58);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(154,110,58);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)\">~</span> y1 <span style=\"color:rgb(154,110,58);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)\">+</span> a<span style=\"color:rgb(154,110,58);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)\">*</span>y2 <span style=\"color:rgb(154,110,58);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)\">+</span> b<span style=\"color:rgb(154,110,58);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)\">*</span>y3 <span style=\"color:rgb(154,110,58);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)\">+</span> c<span style=\"color:rgb(154,110,58);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)\">*</span>y4\r\n     dem65 <span style=\"color:rgb(154,110,58);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(154,110,58);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)\">~</span> y5 <span style=\"color:rgb(154,110,58);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)\">+</span> a<span style=\"color:rgb(154,110,58);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)\">*</span>y6 <span style=\"color:rgb(154,110,58);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)\">+</span> b<span style=\"color:rgb(154,110,58);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)\">*</span>y7 <span style=\"color:rgb(154,110,58);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)\">+</span> c<span style=\"color:rgb(154,110,58);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)\">*</span>y8\r\n\r\n  <span style=\"color:slategray\"># regress mediator on predictor</span>\r\n    dem60 <span style=\"color:rgb(154,110,58);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)\">~</span> ind60\r\n  <span style=\"color:slategray\"># define factor for mediator-residual</span>\r\n    dem60r =<span style=\"color:rgb(154,110,58);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)\">~</span> 1*dem60</font></span></span></div><div><font face=\"Courier New\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);background:none;white-space:pre;word-break:normal;line-height:1.5;overflow:auto\"><span style=\"background:none;word-spacing:normal;word-break:normal;line-height:1.5\">    dem60r ~~ 0*ind60 + 0*dem65 <span style=\"color:rgb(112,128,144)\"># orthogonal to other factors</span>\r\n    dem60  ~~ 0*dem60 <span style=\"color:rgb(112,128,144)\"># set </span></span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(112,128,144);white-space:pre\">variance of </span><span style=\"color:rgb(112,128,144);background-color:initial;word-spacing:normal;white-space:pre\">&quot;automatic&quot; residual to 0</span></font></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);background:none;white-space:pre;word-break:normal;line-height:1.5;overflow:auto\"><span style=\"background:none;word-spacing:normal;word-break:normal;line-height:1.5\"><font face=\"Courier New\">  <span style=\"color:slategray\"># regress outcome on mediator-residual</span><br>    dem65 <span style=\"color:rgb(154,110,58);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)\">~</span> dem60r\r\n&#39;\r\nfit <span style=\"color:rgb(154,110,58);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)\">&lt;-</span> sem<span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,153)\">(</span>model<span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,153)\">,</span> data <span style=\"color:rgb(154,110,58);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.5)\">=</span> PoliticalDemocracy<span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,153)\">)</span></font></span></span><br></div><div><br></div><div>Be careful about your interpretation.  The results could be quite misleading, depending on what your model is doing.</div><div><br></div><div><div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792415127154000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3xn1sJ47isc3h_3Q9nKB5P\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34)\"></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
